{"answer":"Quarterly redemptions as of the last business day of any calendar quarter, on at least 65 days' prior written notice. Redemptions effective within 12 months of an investor's initial subscription incur a 3% early redemption fee, retained by the Fund (not payable to the Adviser) and not applicable to Class E interests. An investor-level gate applies: aggregate redemptions as of any quarter-end may be limited to 20% of the Fund's net asset value. In addition, 90% of proceeds are ordinarily paid within 30 days after the redemption date, with a 10% holdback on a full redemption pending completion of the annual audit.","source_document":"05_fee_schedule.md","section":"Section 5.1 Redemption Terms and Section 5.2 Early Redemption Fee","quote":"Interests in the Flagship Fund and shares of the Offshore Fund may be redeemed as of the last business day of any calendar quarter on at least 65 days' prior written notice. Each Fund may limit aggregate redemptions as of any quarter-end to 20% of its net asset value. Ninety percent of redemption proceeds are ordinarily paid within 30 days after the redemption date, and a holdback of 10% applies to a full redemption until completion of the annual audit. Investors in the Co-Investment Fund have no redemption rights.

### 5.2 Early Redemption Fee

A redemption effective within 12 months after an investor's initial subscription is subject to an early redemption fee of 3% of the amount redeemed. The fee is retained by the Fund for the benefit of remaining investors and is not paid to the Adviser. The fee does not apply to Class E interests."}

